# Architecture rules for the `arch` check. One rule per line:
#   <directory> :: <extended regex> :: <message>
# Every .swift file under <directory> is searched; any matching line is a violation.
# Start with one or two rules you are sure about, add more after real failures.
#
# Examples (uncomment and adjust paths to your project):
#
# Domain stays pure Swift: no UI or persistence frameworks
# Sources/Domain :: ^[[:space:]]*import[[:space:]]+(SwiftUI|UIKit|CoreData|SwiftData) :: Domain must not import UI or persistence frameworks
#
# Domain does not know outer layers (works when layers are separate modules / SPM targets)
# Sources/Domain :: ^[[:space:]]*import[[:space:]]+(Data|Features) :: Domain must not depend on Data or Features
#
# Features reach data only through domain ports, not concrete repositories
# Sources/Features :: [A-Za-z]+RepositoryImpl :: Features must depend on protocols, not implementations
#
# Note: import-based rules work when layers are modules. For folder-only layering, match the
# type names or the paths you want to forbid, or write XCTest-based architecture tests and put them
# in the `unit` step.
